WEBVTT

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.980
Miyashita-san, I saw the news 
about the Saio-dai!

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.890
I'm so grateful...

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.740
I just knew they'd pick you 
someday, Miyashita-san.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.630
It's been such an honor.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.370
How wonderful!

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.480
<b>Annual Saio-dai Chosen</b>

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.840
Miyashita Saori-san, 
Miyashita Textiles Heiress

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.760
This year's Saio-dai... 
Miyashita Saori-san?

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.730
She looks familiar...

00:00:54.450 --> 00:01:00.030
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:16.190
"In Days of Aoi"

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:16.190
Episode Two

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.750
Has that article caught your interest?

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.200
Oh, um, yes...

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.950
B-But... what's the Saio-dai?

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.430
It's the starring role of the Aoi Festival,

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.370
a tradition that dates 
back to the Heian period.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.960
Is being the Saio-dai bad?

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.970
No, it's the highest honor a 
woman of Kyoto can receive.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.470
Th-The highest honor?

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:46.580
Yes. The title is only bestowed upon 
the woman considered foremost

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:50.480
<b>Wisdom</b>

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:50.480
<b>Grace</b>

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:50.480
<b>Social 
Standing</b>

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.160
in wisdom, grace, and social standing.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:56.230
Oh, I realized how you knew 
my house was in Shimogamo!

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.930
Close to Shimogamo Shrine?

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.990
Did you?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.200
Because there are 
a lot of things named "Aoi" there!

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:06.350
<b>Aoi Park</b>

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:06.350
<b>Aoi Elementary</b>

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.350
<b>Aoi Bookstore</b>

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.350
<b>Aoi Crafts</b>

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.250
All of those are named 
after the Aoi Festival.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.250
<b>Aoi Park</b>

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.250
<b>Aoi Elementary</b>

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.250
<b>Aoi Bookstore</b>

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.250
<b>Aoi Crafts</b>

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.250
The festival is held near 
the Shimogamo Shrine, right?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:15.940
So since my name is Aoi too, 
you assumed I lived in the area, right?

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.350
That's right.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.780
There are several events 
associated with the Aoi Festival

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.760
that take place over the course of the month.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.440
But the main event is May 15th,

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.680
when a parade of people 
dressed in period clothing

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:31.160
proceeds from the Kyoto Palace
 to Shimogamo Shrine.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.200
<b>Kyoto Palace</b>

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.770
The centerpiece of said 
parade is the Saio-dai.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.370
<b>Shimogamo Shrine</b>

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:34.770
<b>Kamigamo Shrine</b>

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.370
Priestesses with imperial blood who served

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:40.800
at the Kamo and Ise Shrines 
were known as "Saio."

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.780
For modern festivals, 
a stand-in Saio is chosen.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:48.790
<b>Stand-in Saio</b>

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:48.790
<b>Saio-dai</b>

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:48.790
Oh, I see! So the Saio-dai is 
a stand-in for the Saio.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.980
Hey, Kiyotaka.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:52.540
Owner...

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.760
Are you here to start more trouble?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.540
That's my grandson.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:02.050
Are you the one who brought this family?

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.090
Go right ahead.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.050
Thank you for having us.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.310
Are you Mashiro-san from Class 1?

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.070
Y-Yeah...

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.810
And you're Miyashita-san from Class 2, right?

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:20.820
Yeah, Miyashita Kaori. 
What're you doing here?

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.320
I-I work here part-time...

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:28.290
Oh, you're friends with Miyashita-san's 
younger daughter, eh?

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:31.130
Go on, Miyashita-san.
 Have yourselves a seat.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:33.330
Kiyotaka, you make us some tea.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:41.050
Congratulations to Miyashita Textiles.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.510
Much obliged.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:46.300
My daughter's dreamed of bein' 
Saio-dai for quite a while now.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:50.310
<i>Saori-san's the Saio-dai... 
I thought she looked familiar.</i>

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.320
<i>She's Miyashita-san's big sister.</i>

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:59.820
Have you come here on a matter 
relating to the Saio-dai, perhaps?

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:05.510
Saori-san's been receivin' threatening letters.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.810
Threatening letters?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.830
Yes...

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.330
Allow me to take a look.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:29.850
"You're unfit to be the Saio-dai. Quit at once."

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:38.600
"Quit already. No one likes you."

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:42.610
Was this the first one that you received?

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:46.110
Yes. It was in my bag.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.110
Your bag?

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:51.240
Yes. I had just gotten home from university.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.970
That's when I found that envelope
 I'd never seen before.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:56.440
Did you go anywhere that day
 other than university?

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.120
Flower arrangement lessons.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:02.130
But this other letter 
didn't come in an envelope?

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:08.130
No, that one was just in my bag as is.

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:10.140
I see.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.890
It arrived some time after 
I received the first one.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:17.860
I spoke with Mother about what to do,

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:21.930
but nothing else happened for a while.
Then, just when we began to breathe easy...

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:28.150
Saori-san, would I be correct in assuming 
that you think you know who wrote these?

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:30.910
Wh-What makes you think that?

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:36.730
For someone receiving threatening 
letters, you seem rather calm.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.390
It suggests that the matter 
isn't a complete mystery to you.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:42.850
A part of you is thinking, 
"Ah, I bet <i>that's</i> who it was."

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:44.950
Am I right?

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.920
Sissy, you think maybe it was them?

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:50.930
"Them"?

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.930
There's some girls who hate my sis.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:02.440
A pair of girls with whom 
I was close in high school...

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:06.190
One's family ran a traditional inn, 
while the other's ran a restaurant.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.700
Are those the girls who were 
leavin' you out all the time?

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:13.380
Yeah! And you barged into their 
houses and bellowed at 'em,

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:15.700
which made 'em hate Sissy even more!

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.450
Is that right?

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:23.160
Things got even worse between us after that.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:28.460
Until a few days ago, 
we hadn't even spoken to each other.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:28.460
<b>Hanamura School 
of Flower Arrangement</b>

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:32.970
I have the most delightful 
news for all of you.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:36.970
Someone in our class has been 
chosen to be the Saio-dai!

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:43.660
You hear that? The Saio-dai, she says!

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:46.480
My heart's just gonna burst!

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.990
It's Miyashita Saori-san.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.650
Th-Thank you...

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:10.460
I'll never forget the looks 
on their faces in that moment.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:13.860
Sissy...

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:19.470
An' she says they've been actively 
bullyin' her since then.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:20.970
I see...

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:24.480
Might I speak to them myself?

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:28.000
Do you mean to ask if they're behind this?

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:32.990
No. I wouldn't reveal the fact 
that I've spoken with you.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.310
Well, this weekend,

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:39.990
our class will be exhibiting our flower 
arrangements at a nearby hotel.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.570
All of the students will be there.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.740
I see. That sounds ideal.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:51.260
Aoi-san, there's a cafe in that hotel 
that serves delicious French toast.

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:03.270
Aoi-san. Has the younger sister, Kaori-san, 
said anything to you at school?

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.270
I'm beggin' you!

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:09.270
Yes, though she told me not to tell anyone.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:12.610
Not that I was intending to...

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:17.530
You don't have any friends 
at school that you can trust?

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.720
W-Well...

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:36.550
Aoi-san?

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:38.660
Aoi-san?

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:42.900
Flowers can have therapeutic properties.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.930
<b>Hanamura
Flower Arrangement Exhibition</b>

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:45.930
As long as we're here,

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:48.440
we should enjoy the exhibit.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.090
Yeah!

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.330
They're all so wonderful!

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:58.360
Yes, I'm very glad that we came.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.350
These two pieces...

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:09.710
Such a difference in quality, isn't there?

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:14.460
Oh, Hanamura-sensei!

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:17.620
My, my! Is that Seiji-san's grandson, Kiyotaka-kun?

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:18.970
Haven't you grown!

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.540
<i>They know each other?</i>

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:23.970
Are these the work of the Saio-dai?

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:27.610
She made the larger one in the classroom.

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:30.980
She made the smaller one at home.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.860
Isn't the smaller one so much finer?

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:38.550
Yes. Young people create such vibrant art.

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:40.740
Do you have any other works by her peers?

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:47.500
There are two other students in my class 
who attend university with Miyashita-san.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:56.250
Oh, heck...

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.110
What a catch!

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.760
He's comin' over!

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:05.220
Kiyotaka-kun, allow me to introduce 
Mikami Yuko-san and Kawase Keiko-san.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.770
A p-pleasure!

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:11.070
The pleasure is all mine. 
My name is Yagashira Kiyotaka,

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:15.020
and this is my part-time 
co-worker, Mashiro Aoi-san.

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:21.530
Your energy truly comes through in your art.

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:29.040
And Sensei, you must be elated that one of 
your students was chosen as the Saio-dai.

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:35.790
Pardon me. My phone is ringing.

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.270
Kiyotaka-kun's such a busy young man.

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:42.020
Mashiro-san, do enjoy the rest of your visit.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.890
<i>Ask Keiko-san and Yuko-san 
all kinds of questions, okay?</i>

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.890
<b>Thanks!</b>

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:52.520
<i>Hang on!</i>

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:53.900
Say, Mashiro-san...

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:55.080
Y-Yes?!

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.450
Are you datin' that hottie?

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:59.630
N-No! We're just co-workers.

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:02.690
Thank goodness! Hunks like him 
don't just fall outta the sky.

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:05.570
We'd better get in good before he meets <i>her</i>!

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:07.090
"Her"?

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:09.830
Miyashita Saori, this year's Saio-dai!

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.370
She's freakin' gorgeous, y'know?

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.150
The guys're always flockin' to her.

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:15.080
And she's always takin' all the best ones.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:21.090
I guess it must be frustrating to have 
the Saio-dai be someone from your class...

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:23.870
Bein' around her's always been frustrating.

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:26.740
Guys have always preferred her over us.

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:31.770
But with her family's business in decline, 
her gettin' named Saio-dai is...

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:35.250
Knowin' her mom's ego, 
she'll follow through even if it ruins her.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.890
Now... give us the scoop on that guy already!

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:42.360
Oh... he's...

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:45.110
Despite how he looks, 
he's actually quite strange.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:54.620
I beg your pardon, Aoi-san.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.810
I-I'm very sorry, Holmes-san!

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:07.720
I didn't mean "strange" in a bad way...

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.140
I meant more like "extraordinary"!

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:09.870
Aoi-san.

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:11.640
Would you mind paying?

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:18.650
I'm joking with you, Aoi-san.

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:23.140
Kyoto boys <i>are</i> nasty...

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:30.660
Aoi-san, you said that once before, but the 
saying is about "Kyoto men," not "Kyoto boys."

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.400
Oh, was it?

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:36.920
But you feel more like a 
"Kyoto boy" than a "Kyoto man."

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:43.530
That's not how it goes. Though I suppose 
"Kyoto boy" does have a lighter feel to it.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:47.480
Now, were Keiko-san and Yuko-san forthcoming?

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.770
Yes, a lot more than I expected...

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:56.430
I see. So they were entirely open 
about their resentment for Saori-san?

00:13:56.430 --> 00:14:00.190
Yeah, I honestly couldn't believe how 
eager they were to talk about it.

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:11.030
It's so nice out here...

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:15.770
Have you learned anything?

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:16.910
I believe so.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:18.950
I'd like to speak with you at length.

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:20.670
Do you have any free time tomorrow?

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.290
Um, tomorrow is...

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.670
She's gotta be at Shimogamo Shrine tomorrow.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:27.180
When is your appointment?

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:28.750
Nine o'clock.

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:31.000
Then why don't we meet in the

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.930
Tadasu-no-Mori Forest on the 
Shimogamo Shrine grounds at 8?

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:36.760
I'll tell you everything then.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:45.690
Holmes-san, you said "everything"... 
But what's this about?

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:50.130
About who sent this letter, of course.

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:53.740
Good morning!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:56.240
You're up early, Aoi-san.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:58.450
Well, I do live nearby...

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:01.010
Your eyes are a bit red.

00:15:01.010 --> 00:15:03.960
Were you so curious about the 
case that you couldn't sleep?

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:07.010
O-Of course I was. Who wouldn't be?

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.640
Indeed.

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:13.010
And it seems a few other interested 
parties have arrived as well.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.780
Good mornin' to you.

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:17.620
Good morning to you, too.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:20.770
Forgive me for calling you out so early.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:25.010
So, do you know who's sendin' 
those threatening letters?

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.870
The one who wrote this letter...

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:35.280
was you, Kaori-san.

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:39.040
Wh-What makes you think that?

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:43.040
Yeah! Those two girls got 
way more motive than I do!

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:47.550
Being the Saio-dai costs money.

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:49.180
Money?

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:50.050
Yes.

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:54.650
It is said that preparations to serve as 
the Saio-dai can cost as much as 10 million yen.

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:57.180
T-Ten million?!

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:02.280
Kaori-san, you attend 
Ohki High School with Aoi-san,

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:05.220
even though your sister attends 
a prestigious private university.

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:08.690
You chose to attend public school because

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:11.440
you were worried about your 
family's finances, weren't you?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:17.130
But with her family's business in decline, 
her gettin' named Saio-dai is...

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:20.450
Knowin' her mom's ego, 
she'll follow through even if it ruins her!

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:23.480
When Saori-san was named the Saio-dai,

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.880
you became worried for your 
family's future, didn't you?

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:29.460
That's right!

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:33.220
Our family's been in business for ages, 
but we keep losin' money lately!

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:36.590
I knew Mommy and Daddy 
wouldn't turn the offer down,

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:41.070
so I wrote those threatening letters, 
hopin' it would give 'em an excuse to decline.

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:42.730
<b>You're unfit to be the Saio-dai. 
Quit at once.</b>

00:16:41.070 --> 00:16:42.730
But...

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.850
They didn't use that excuse.

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:48.840
Yeah. I finished the threatening letter,

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:50.360
but I started havin' second thoughts...

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:53.670
I heard my parents talkin' about how

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:58.160
it costs money to be the Saio-dai, 
but it'd pay for itself in publicity...

00:16:58.160 --> 00:16:59.370
Kaori...

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.880
So you put the letter into your own bag.

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:05.010
Didn't you, Saori-san?

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.380
You mean it?

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:12.880
But why? You were so glad to be the Saio-dai...

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:18.390
On the contrary. Saori-san wrote
 the second letter herself.

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:28.150
How did you know?

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:30.900
Your two exhibits at the flower show.

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:37.660
The smaller piece created at home was made 
not by you, but by Kaori-san, wasn't it?

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.420
You could tell?

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:44.160
Sensei mentioned a difference in quality, 
but there was more to it than that.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:49.030
They were clearly made by different people.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:50.170
Different people?

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:54.170
Works of different quality, 
said to be by the same person...

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:56.720
The threatening letters were the same way.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:00.180
The first seems to have been 
put together with great care,

00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:03.810
but the second one doesn't 
have the same effort put into it.

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.300
Two people made those flower arrangements.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:08.610
And two people made those 
threatening letters.

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:12.820
I could see the two of you
 reflected in each of them.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.820
And I think you both wrote them
 for different reasons.

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:20.820
I wanted us to be friends again, like before...

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:25.370
Keiko and Yuko have been 
avoiding me since high school...

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.580
I thought that once I was chosen as Saio-dai,

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:32.850
they'd be happy for me 
and we could be friends again.

00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:36.230
But it just made them hate me even more.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:40.710
I thought that if I was 
receiving threatening letters,

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:42.870
they'd get worried and be nice to me...

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:46.600
Sissy, you jerk!

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:52.120
I thought you were worryin' 
about the family, like me!

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:54.370
But you were doin' it over 
somethin' that stupid?

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.490
You don't know what I'm goin' through!

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:59.610
You don't know how it feels, 
always bein' left out!

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.240
You bet I don't!

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:05.240
Why do you care so much about 
what those jerks think?

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.050
They don't get how great you are!

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:10.330
They're always sayin' bad stuff 
about you! So just forget 'em!

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.530
Be the most beautiful Saio-dai there is.

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:18.330
Then become such an amazin' woman so that, 
someday, those two will start braggin',

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:22.140
"I used to be friends with her!"

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:25.510
Kaori...

00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:32.290
That was magnificent, Kaori-san.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:38.580
Saori-san, I agree with what Kaori-san said.

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:44.410
Please become a radiant Saio-dai 
that will mesmerize everyone.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:46.780
Okay!

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:50.570
Now, Miyashita-san, 
I feel I should return these.

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:53.060
Gracious me! How embarrassing...

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:55.920
Thank you so much.

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:59.700
Kiyotaka-san, I can't apologize enough.

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:01.930
Me neither...

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:04.420
Think nothing of it.

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:07.060
Anyway, I believe it's time, isn't it?

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:08.760
Oh, you said it!

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:11.060
Mommy, we oughta go.

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:15.340
Kiyotaka-san, if you would please be so kind...

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:19.070
Don't worry. I wouldn't dream
 of mentioning this to anyone.

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:21.970
Well, we'd best get going, then.

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:31.830
Kaori-san!

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:37.280
Um...

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:41.490
There's a cafe in a famous hotel 
that serves great French toast...

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:46.720
Want to go there with me sometime?

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:51.460
Sure thing! Let's grab a bite sometime!

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:54.230
Thank you!

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:58.770
Bye-bye!

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:03.530
Bye-bye!

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:05.990
Isn't that nice?

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:09.620
When you meet someone you know 
you want to be friends with.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:13.270
It is.

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:48.500
Saori-san's so pretty...

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:14.240
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:52.000
Next Episode

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:52.000
"The Case of the Mt. Kurama Estate Inheritance"

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:38.790
It's Kurama! Kurama!

00:23:38.790 --> 00:23:40.200
You think I'll meet a tengu?

00:23:40.200 --> 00:23:44.330
No tengu, but you may meet a handsome 
man filled with overwhelming arrogance.

00:23:44.820 --> 00:23:48.140
Next time: "The Case of the 
Mt. Kurama Estate Inheritance"

00:23:48.140 --> 00:23:50.400
Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
